course: dictionary
lesson: 9284
title: One word, many meanings: spare
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and spare is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «Mum has £80 for the shop, so there is £4 spare» means £4 left over, not being used.
explain: «Live shows keep spare costumes ready» means extra costumes, kept in case they are needed. Ask yourself: is something extra, free, or left over here? Then try that meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Spare can also be a verb. «Can you spare a pencil?» means can you give one you do not need. «The king spared the dragon's life» means he did not hurt it. The words around spare, such as a thing, a time, or a person, are your clues.
fact: Spare has several meanings, so check the sentence to find the right one.
fact: «A spare tyre» means an extra one, kept in case it is needed.
fact: «Spare time» means free time when you are not working.
fact: «To spare» means left over, as in «we got there with ten minutes to spare».
fact: «To spare someone» means to not hurt them, or to save them from something.
exercise: «Live shows keep spare costumes ready.» What does spare mean here? | Hidden under the stage | *Extra, kept in case it is needed | Old and broken | Very quiet
exercise: «Mum has £80 for the shop, so there is £4 spare.» What does spare mean? | Missing and lost | Owed to the shop | *Left over, not being used | Given to a friend
exercise: «Can you spare a pencil?» What does spare mean here? | To hurt someone badly | To be late | Ready to fight | *To give something you do not need
test: «The king spared the dragon's life.» What does spared mean? | Gave a gift | Ran away from it | *Did not hurt it, saved it from harm | Kept it safe in a box
test: «The family offered a spare room to their guests.» What does spare room mean? | A room for storing old toys | A room that is always locked | *An extra room not used every day by the family | A tiny room under the stairs
exam: Ella asks, «Spare can mean extra, free or left over, so how do I know which one?» What is the best answer? | *Read the words around it and try each meaning in the sentence | Spare means the same thing every time | Always pick the first meaning in the dictionary | Ask a dog
